WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.567
-The Oscars were last night.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.200
Here to talk about it is
one of our writers,

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.834
Amber Ruffin, with her very own
Oscars recap!

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:10.400
[ Applause ]
-Yay!

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.634
Hey, everybody. Hey, Seth.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:16.167
You guys, there is nothing like
the magic of the Oscars,

00:00:16.167 --> 00:00:17.901
and last night was no exception.

00:00:17.901 --> 00:00:19.000
First things first --

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.801
Beyoncé's performance
was breathtaking.

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:23.834
Her song about how good it is
to be alive

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:26.167
made me feel
so good to be alive.

00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:29.801
It just filled me with hope, a
hope that would never dissipate.

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:32.834
Then, Troy Kotsur won
for "CODA" and Seth,

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:35.567
when the audience stood up
and applauded in sign for him,

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:36.968
it was quite the moment --

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:40.067
a moment that would surely
be the focus of the evening.

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:41.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.501 --> 00:00:44.200
Then, during a performance of
"We Don't Talk About Bruno,"

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.267
Megan Thee Stallion rapped,
and it was heaven.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:49.067
It's things like these
that make you feel like

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:51.667
you're having a moment
with all of America.

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:53.801
And then, here's a sentence

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:55.934
we will say
for the rest of our lives --

00:00:55.934 --> 00:00:57.767
Will Smith slapped Chris Rock.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:00.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.434 --> 00:01:03.334
And life as we know it
changed forever.

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:04.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:06.200
I had hoped that it was a bit,

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.567
but that hope quickly
turned to dust.

00:01:08.567 --> 00:01:13.701
A dark sadness filled my home,
a darkness I couldn't escape.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:16.067
Had the Oscars lost its magic?

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:19.234
My sister, Lacey, called me,
and we screamed.

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:22.934
We screamed a long, loud scream
of excitement?

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:24.834
Terror? I don't know.

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:27.167
But we screamed it
with all of America.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.734
We tried to stay engaged,

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:31.801
but there was no more show
after that.

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:33.968
There was no more anything!

00:01:33.968 --> 00:01:36.033
The once-fluffy couch
I was sitting on

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:39.033
suddenly felt like
hard and unwelcoming.

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.133
My heated blanket went cool.

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:45.567
The sweet tea I was enjoying
lost all its flavor.

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:48.133
The Oscars took everything
I thought I knew

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.801
and flushed it down the toilet.

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:54.067
In this new world,
could I survive?

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:58.667
I know now why they don't have a
category for Best Horror Movie,

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:04.400
because the best horror movie
is the Oscars.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:07.100
Lacey called back,
this time with FaceTime.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:09.567
I needed to see
her screaming face

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:11.300
to know I wasn't dreaming.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:12.734
And then it happened.

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:17.467
The announcer said, "And the
Oscar for Best Actor goes to..."

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:20.834
and all of America collectively
held their breath,

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:22.334
bit their cuticles,

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:26.400
and then Will Smith won
for Best Actor!

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:32.334
His acceptance speech lasted for
5 minutes and 25 seconds,

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:38.100
and I did not breathe for
5 minutes and 25 seconds!

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.968
The Earth cracked open
and I slipped through.

00:02:41.968 --> 00:02:46.167
I heard echoes of "I'm sorry,
but never to Chris Rock"?

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:49.534
I -- I'm not sure what he said,
because again,

00:02:49.534 --> 00:02:52.267
I'm in the center of the Earth
at this point.

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:55.167
It comes to an end,
and I scroll Twitter

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:58.834
and I read jokes and thinkpieces
and opinions about it,

00:02:58.834 --> 00:03:03.200
and while I felt like I had seen
something horrible and private

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.767
that made me feel great shame,

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:09.434
I found out everyone in America
felt the same way I did.

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:10.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:13.501
And that, my friends,
is the magic of the Oscars!

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:15.801
[ Sparkling sound ]

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:18.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:28.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:33.868
-Amber Ruffin, everybody!

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:35.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

